# Agent Guardrails

## No unsolicited changes to the repository

- NEVER push commits, create branches, or open PRs unless the user explicitly says "go ahead", "execute", "implement it", or similar unambiguous confirmation.
- Creating Linear tickets, updating ticket status, and other project management actions are OK when requested.
- When the user asks you to "make" or "add" something, clarify whether they want a plan/proposal or actual execution before touching any files.
- Confirm with the user before updating statuses or closing Linear tickets.
- Linear tickets should not be verbose for this project. Maximum of 4-5 bullet points are sufficient per ticket description.

## Default to planning

- When in doubt, present a plan and ask for confirmation before writing code, committing, or pushing.
- Treat "can you do X?" as a request to plan X, not to execute X.
- Always show the user what you intend to commit before committing.

## Git safety

- Never push to main/master.
- Never force push.
- Never amend commits that have been pushed.
